  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1118 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nAn upper level high will build in over the next few days with \ngradually warming surface temperatures. Highs will increase into the \n70s and eventually approach 80 F for some areas by late in the week. \nA transient upper level disturbance will round the high pressure \narea late Monday into Tuesday, bringing an increase in clouds and \nslowing the warm up slightly. NBM had no Pops, but a few models \nindicated at least a slight chance, so added a token 5 percent pop \nnorth of I-40. Otherwise conditions will be dry until this weekend. \nAt that time a weakening Pacific trough may eject through the \nregion. Some guidance pulls up sufficient subtropical moisture for \nshowers and storms while other models do not. So this is a low \nconfidence outlook at this time, but meaningful rainfall will not \noccur until at least then.",
